<title>UK: Caradon in talks to sell auto plastics unit.</title>
<headline>Caradon in talks to sell auto plastics unit.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-08-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Building products to automotive components manufacturer Caradon Plc on Friday said it was in discussions with a leading North American automotive components supplier over selling its Rolinx automotive plastics businesses.</p>
<p>No financial details were mentioned. In the year ended 31 December 1995, these businesses reported turnover of 68 million stg and had a year-end net tangible asset value of 15.8 million stg, the company said in a statement.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
